1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Construction teams already have permit portals. The expensive work begins when a digital record becomes stale or conflicts with the human process.

2
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:16,000
PermitDiff is an exception resolver that knows when not to call and refuses to invent administrative authority.

3
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:27,000
It first freezes the portal snapshot and applies a deterministic no-call gate. Fresh and consistent records finish without constructing a CALL-E request.

4
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:38,000
Only staleness or an explicit conflict makes one authorized, bounded phone check eligible. Every outcome remains tied to the same snapshot.

5
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:48,000
For a fresh record, the correct product outcome is no call needed. Avoiding unnecessary phone work is a visible success state.

6
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:59,000
For a stale record, grounded phone evidence may verify that the office-reported status still matches the frozen portal snapshot.

7
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:12,000
When the phone evidence differs, PermitDiff surfaces a discrepancy for human review. The official record never changes and official confirmation stays required.

8
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:24,000
CALL-E asks only for factual status, missing items, the next procedural step, and an office reference tied to the exact synthetic permit case.

9
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:36,000
Accepted evidence binds the call ID, case, permit, exact destination, jurisdiction, snapshot hash, confidence, and recipient-side corroboration.

10
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:46,000
The authority boundary is load-bearing: a phone answer can open an exception, but it cannot approve a permit or overwrite municipal truth.

11
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:57,000
Wrong office, no consent, voicemail, ambiguity, low confidence, malformed output, or missing grounding fails closed and blocks blind redial.

12
00:01:57,120 --> 00:02:08,000
CALL-E maintainers reviewed the implementation and merged pull request one ninety-nine into the official community repository.

13
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:20,000
The project passes fifty-three tests above a ninety-percent coverage gate, including the published SDK create-call and polling boundary.

14
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:30,000
The current reviewer paths are deterministic and clearly labeled. A real provider pilot will be claimed only after an authorized, consented validation succeeds.
